# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — vLLM CPU image
# =============================================================================
# Each entry is a HIGH finding that is NOT reachable by the running inference
# server. They live in build/packaging tooling (setuptools' bundled _vendor
# dir, or pip's vendored deps) that vLLM never imports at serve time. The
# active runtime packages are patched (see the Dockerfile CVE-remediation
# layer: setuptools is pinned to the fixed 78.1.1). We suppress the
# build-time/vendored copies with justification rather than mutate the
# internals of setuptools/pip (which risks breaking package tooling) or pull
# setuptools past vLLM's supported range (<81.0.0).
#
# Review cadence: re-evaluate when the vLLM base image is bumped.
# =============================================================================

# setuptools: active version is 78.1.1 (the fixed release). The flagged 70.3.0
# is a stale/vendored METADATA copy, not the imported package.
CVE-2025-47273

# wheel 0.45.1 — bundled inside setuptools/_vendor (build-time only, not a
# runtime import path for the inference server).
CVE-2026-24049

# jaraco.context 5.3.0 — bundled inside setuptools/_vendor (build-time only).
CVE-2026-23949

# msgpack 1.1.2 — vendored inside pip (pip/_vendor). Used only by pip during
# dependency resolution, never by the running vLLM server. No standalone
# msgpack is installed; upgrading is not possible without patching pip itself.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
